x86_64-linux  clang lowers the zeroing of the larger class to a call it invents - memset - where cxx1 writes the member stores itself, so clang's name set has memset in it and cxx1's does not. A helper a compiler chooses is not an ABI name. arm64-darwin agrees on every name.
x86_64-windows  the same memset, for the same reason.
